      "mergedPostDetails": "1. Create three separate gameobjects\n\n2. Put a vrc rotation constraint on number 2.\n\n3. Set the rotation constraint up as follows:\n\n- First source: object 1, weight 0\n\n- Second source: object 2, weight 1\n\n- Third source: object 3, weight 0.15\n\n4. Give object 3 a slight tilt.\n\nYou will see  object 2 slowly rotate before snapping back, instead of slowly rotating towards the rotation of object 3 and staying there. This breaks the Rotation Synced version of the VRLabs Rigidbody Throw.\n\nThe settings: https://i.imgur.com/h17pSqq.png\n\nLink to prefab: https://files.jellejurre.dev/ShareX/VRC-Rotation-Constraint-Bug-Example.prefab\n\nExample of bug: https://files.jellejurre.dev/ShareX/2024-07-24%2022-41-56.mp4",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[SDK3.6.2-constraints.2] Rotation damping constraint breaks with another zero source",
