  "details": "**How to reproduce**\n\n1. Place three GameObjects in the scene as shown in the hierarchy below.\n\n```\n\n+ (AvatarRoot)\n\n    + Dummy\n\n    + Controller\n\n    + Target\n\n```\n\nTransforms of all objects are (0, 0, 0) position, (0, 0, 0) rotation, and (1, 1, 1) scale.\n\n2. Add VRCRotationConstraint to `Target` and configure sources as shown below and activate it.\n\n```\n\nElement 0:\n\n  Source Transform = Dummy\n\n  Weight = 0\n\nElement 1:\n\n  Source Transform = Target\n\n  Weight = 0.5\n\nElement 2:\n\n  Source Transform = Controller\n\n  Weight = 0.5\n\n```\n\n3. Enter play mode.\n\n4. Rotate `Controller` randomly.\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nThe rotation of `Target` will follow `Controller`'s rotation with slight smoothing.\n\n** Actual behavior**\n\n`Target` may vibrate violently even though `Controller` is stationary.\n\nAlso, it seems that removing Element 0 (Dummy) from VRCRotationConstraint suppresses this problem.\n\n**Environment**\n\n- VRCSDK Avatars 3.6.2-constraints.2",
